# ChangeLog is append-only in practice: every branch adds its own lines
# under the headings for the current cycle, and two branches adding
# entries are not really in conflict.  The built-in "union" merge driver
# resolves such a hunk by keeping the lines from both sides instead of
# leaving conflict markers.
#
# Note that union never reports a conflict, so a genuine disagreement --
# two branches rewording the same line -- silently yields both versions.
# Read the merged ChangeLog before committing a merge.
ChangeLog merge=union
